 ## 7. Comparison with primary cone-volume and stability literature
+
+The class \(\mathcal E_d\) is the familiar class of affine Cartesian products
+of centrally symmetric intervals and planar bodies, called Weil bodies in
+Saroglou, [*On the shape of a convex body with respect to its second projection
+body*](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1409.4347v2), pp. 2–4. That paper relates the class
+to Weil's polytopal classification for homothety under the second projection-body
+operator and gives a three-dimensional zonoid endpoint with symmetric-cylinder
+equality (Theorem 1.2). These use a different functional from \(a(K)\); the
+common extremal class alone does not make their statements equivalent to
+entry005 v4's equality theorem or Theorem A here.
 
